{"title":"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (answer choices)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the set of fractions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c16e139d3e9cec6bebe546e0ec21182d902199.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{3}{2}, \\frac{6}{7}, \\frac{3}{5}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" />. Ordered from smallest to largest, the set is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/a/63ad0e006b9a3cd5b57da7c5148169df787cdde2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{6}{7}, \\frac{3}{2}\\} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\{\\frac{3}{2}, \\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{6}{7}, \\frac{3}{7}\\} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\{\\frac{3}{2}, \\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{6}{7}\\} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\{\\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{6}{7}, \\frac{3}{2}\\}\\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{3}{2}, \\frac{6}{7}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"816\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can give everything a common denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. This gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/48730ccc8d06c96ffdc7ef0f5812e105b998ef14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{7} = \\frac{3 \\times 10}{7 \\times 10} = \\frac{30}{70}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"139\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef4a7697cb76b82b7b60f1bf802bcb3089270b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2} = \\frac{3 \\times 35}{2 \\times 35} = \\frac{105}{70}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"148\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c6a96fba141bab5af2116cffca088913967ad5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{7} = \\frac{6 \\times 10}{7 \\times 10} = \\frac{60}{70}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"139\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/1/781ff0ac4a279fd77d7a526cd130f76f42faad78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5} = \\frac{3 \\times 14}{5 \\times 14} = \\frac{42}{70}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"139\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Ordering these from least to greatest by comparing their numerators (since their denominators are now all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa94edfb9739dcc66dad90f7dd5c148f44a57e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />), we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/436609bafedcc510b8a22db103c58537c7d0d87a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{ (A) }\\ \\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{6}{7}, \\frac{3}{2}\\}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"155\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/9679889a5cfb269afb9b32462fee5417e6b62956.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2} &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" /> because its numerator is more than its denominator, but all of the other numbers are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because their denominators are all lower than their numerators. This means it must be the highest.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad197598a8f83e8ba2e1b7fb703713466b65dbad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{7} &lt; \\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"38\" /> because the denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/758a4c1c67be9c9db0c4a808c62384d660579448.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> is greater than the denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac40ce1434cda0943c408cc185f5976212d95801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/f/4efd288cef6006f9390ea9c557d0dd18b46f82bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5} = \\frac{3 \\times 7}{5 \\times 7} = \\frac{21}{35}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"130\" height=\"40\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/79261b1a17779a427034c973428c177f8c9472ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{7} = \\frac{6 \\times 5}{7 \\times 5} = \\frac{30}{35}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"130\" height=\"40\" />, which has a higher numerator but the same denominator than the other fraction. \n</p><p>Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/436609bafedcc510b8a22db103c58537c7d0d87a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{ (A) }\\ \\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{6}{7}, \\frac{3}{2}\\}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"155\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(answer_choices)\">Solution 3 (answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/9679889a5cfb269afb9b32462fee5417e6b62956.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2} &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" /> while the others are less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we know that the answer must be A or D. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad197598a8f83e8ba2e1b7fb703713466b65dbad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{7} &lt; \\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"38\" /> due to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/758a4c1c67be9c9db0c4a808c62384d660579448.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> having a higher denominator, so the answer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/436609bafedcc510b8a22db103c58537c7d0d87a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{ (A) }\\ \\{\\frac{3}{7}, \\frac{3}{5}, \\frac{6}{7}, \\frac{3}{2}\\}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"155\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_